cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CoRTeC: Cohort-Conditioned Differentially Private Synthetic Tabular Data from a Frozen Language Model"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22945316"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Calyie/cortec"
abstract: >-
  Differentially private synthetic tabular data is worth producing only if a model trained on it
  performs as one trained on the real records. The deployed marginal mechanisms, MST and AIM, were
  built for marginal workloads and are evaluated on them; measured instead on this quantity, at
  library defaults and ε = 2 on UCI Adult, their output trains models 0.14 to 0.17 AUC below a
  same-size real sample. CoRTeC spends the privacy budget once, on a release built for a downstream
  model, and trains nothing. Within publicly defined cohorts it publishes one Laplace histogram per
  attribute and outcome class, and a table of target rates over disjoint cells, so conditional
  structure costs one query per level. A frozen language model then decodes the release under exact
  per-bin counts and selection from a pool. It never sees a private record, so generation is post-
  processing: unlimited datasets at no further privacy cost. At ε = 2 and n = 300, no model trained
  on CoRTeC's output separates from one trained on a real sample of the same size on census or
  credit data, one tree model is 0.05 AUC short on clinical data, and 1-way marginal error is
  within 0.005 of MST's on the first two and below it on the third. The gap lies largely in what is
  released: giving MST and AIM a private conditional table recovers most of it at no change to
  either mechanism. Four membership-inference attacks validated on a positive control reach at most
  0.049 advantage against a permitted 0.762. Both criteria the field selects synthesisers on are
  saturated: real data with its target permuted passes a 90% marginal-similarity bar, and a
  language model given only column names passes aggregate downstream utility on a public benchmark.
  Only conditional and subgroup measures, against a real-sample and a no-information floor,
  separate a mechanism that transmits the institution's structure from one that recites a prior.
